From d59ef739019f2dc12abae80c14c077ef235c8d84 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: seedds <seedds@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 11:14:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 0168: title row 3 back to VR, shop picker replaces the UIKit
 picker, guide tap fix

Revert the 0157 title-menu repurpose: the 0x497314 CUTS NOP, the
0x4972f4 row-3 text cut and the 0x1d7290 confirm-switch intercept are
removed (CUTS is empty again), and the UIKit CharSelectEditor is
deleted (its preview PNGs follow in 0169/0170). Character selection
moves into the in-game shop (0167 data: ItemList rows 0,1,2,
Luigi2D.szs, MSBT labels). The model/costume redirect (hle_fs.c,
0163/0165) and the DmCharSelect.* persistence are unchanged; the
persistence now lives in CharSelectPersist.m, which the launcher still
calls at startup.

0164 is not in the build tree (removed from series), so this patch
deletes nothing for it -- the 0164 probe lines were never there to
remove. (The original 0168 was generated on a tree that still
contained 0164, so its 0164-deletion hunks could not apply to the
real build tree; this regeneration drops them.)

Guide tap fix: DmGamepad.m controlAt: no longer treats the left half
as the floating-stick area while a web page is shown, so the offline
guide's menu items on the left half are tappable (hitTest already
forwards non-control touches to the page).

Note: the shop-picker write-back (0166) is not in this commit; the
confirmed row cannot be identified from static code (see the game
note's Open section).
