-// CharSelectEditor.m -- the title-menu character/costume picker (0157).
-//
-// The picker opens over the title menu when the player picks the
-// "角色选择" row (the repurposed VR row). Three characters (Mario, Luigi,
-// Wario) and their costumes, all at once. Peach / Toad / Pauline are not
-// in this round (no ready models) and are not listed.
-//
-// Style (redone for V1.3.29 to look like the in-game Crazy Cap shop -- the
-// user asked for it directly, "界面做成这种！"):
-//   * OPAQUE: the whole editor is a solid deep-purple panel (the shop's
-//     purple); the title menu does NOT show through behind it. The old
-//     white centred panel over a dimmed menu (which the user called ugly
-//     because it was see-through) is gone.
-//   * LEFT: a big character preview -- a large accent-coloured disc with
-//     the character's first Chinese character, the character name, and
-//     the current outfit (cap + clothes) as a summary. Three character
-//     tabs above it.
-//   * RIGHT: two horizontal costume strips (caps, then clothes). Each card
-//     is a shop-style card: a purple emblem with the costume's first
-//     Chinese character on top (the "image"), the Chinese name below, a
-//     gold frame when selected. "默认" first, "跟随存档" last.
-//   * BELOW the strips: the selected costume's Chinese name + description
-//     (the shop's item name + description area).
-//   * BOTTOM BAR (like the shop's L 选择 / B 放弃 / A 确定): 返回 (close
-//     without saving), 默认 (reset), 选择 (gold: save + apply + close).
-//   * Text uses the game's own font (dm/font/standard.ttf, registered
-//     from DM_FONT_DIR) instead of the iOS system font the other editors
-//     use; it falls back to the system font when the file is missing.
-//   * Costume names + descriptions are the game's own Chinese text
-//     (LocalizedData/CNzh, ItemCap.msbt / ItemCloth.msbt); a costume with
-//     no MSBT name falls back to the cleaned internal name (never a raw
-//     internal name like "ColorWario" on a card).
-//
-// Images: the shop shows a live 3D render of each costume's <Name>2D.szs
-// model on its cards. Those files are 3D models (FMDL + an embedded BNTX
-// holding small dot-pattern textures), not flat portraits -- there is no
-// costume portrait PNG inside them to extract, and the shop layout's
-// __Combined.bntx atlases hold only UI chrome (CmBase, NyShopLogo,
-// NyFrameItem, NyListBeak). So the renders are made OFFLINE instead: the
-// game's own BFRES models are rendered to transparent PNGs on the host
-// (Blender + the ranidspace BFRES importer; REPORT-CHAR-PREVIEW.md) and
-// bundled here as dm/ios/Sources/CharPreviews/*.png, like the PadIcons.
-// A card shows its render when one exists; the drawn emblem (the costume's
-// first Chinese character in gold on purple) is only the fallback for an
-// item with no render (the MarioInvisible cap has no cap file at all, so
-// no render exists for it). The big preview shows the character wearing
-// the selected clothes (the clothes render), or the default outfit;
-// a cap pick does not change it -- a cap+clothes combination has no
-// single render, and the cap itself is shown on its card.
-//
-// Persistence: NSUserDefaults DmCharSelect.character ("mario" | "luigi" |
-// "wario"), DmCharSelect.cap and DmCharSelect.clothes (a costume name, or
-// "default" for the character's own default part, or no key = follow the
-// save). The live channel is setenv/unsetenv DM_CHAR_SELECT /
-// DM_CHAR_CAP / DM_CHAR_CLOTHES (the host fs redirect re-reads getenv on
-// every open, so a pick takes effect at the next spawn). "选择" saves;
-// the launcher applies the saved settings before the game starts
-// (dm_char_select_apply_saved, like DmHudPad.*).
-//
-// Costume lists (from the costume system: a costume is a family of
-// ObjectData/<Name>*.szs; a character only lists the costumes it has
-// adapted versions of, because an unadapted costume loads that
-// costume's Mario body and the player silently becomes Mario again):
-//   Mario: all 55 caps + 55 clothes (the "Mario" entry itself is the
-//     "默认" card, so it is not listed twice).
-//   Luigi: clothes Default + MarioColorLuigi / MarioColorWaluigi /
-//     MarioColorWario; caps Default only (the Luigi mod ships no adapted
-//     cap, so Luigi's cap is Mario's red cap).
-//   Wario: clothes + caps Default + MarioColorWario / MarioColorLuigi /
-//     MarioColorWaluigi / MarioColorClassic / MarioColorGold / Mario64 /
-//     MarioHigh / MarioPilot / MarioPrimitiveMan / MarioCaptain (Captain
-//     is cap+head only; as clothes it gives the Captain head with the
-//     default body).
-//
-// The text is Chinese: the user asked for the settings panel in Chinese
